# The repository is edited on Windows and checked out on Linux. core.autocrlf
# handles ordinary source, but a CRLF here is not a cosmetic difference: a
# trailing \r in a shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter named
# "bash\r", and systemd and nginx both read their config files literally.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# The two ASPIRE story videos, ~185MB together. LFS is not a preference here:
# GitHub hard-rejects any single file over 100MB and Monique's is 108MB, so a
# plain commit is refused outright. They cannot be gitignored either -- the
# deploy is `git reset --hard origin/<branch>` (deploy/update.sh), so a file
# outside the repository never reaches production.
#
# Cloning without git-lfs leaves 130-byte pointer files in their place and the
# video panel serves those instead of video. `git lfs install` once per machine.
frontend/public/videos/*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
